  "notes": "Term-by-term sequence transcribed verbatim from the official 2025-2026 Arkansas Tech University Catalog, 'Electrical Engineering - Biomedical Option, Bachelor of Science' curriculum (pp. 383-385), a genuine institution-published suggested sequence. The BS Electrical Engineering program is accredited by the Engineering Accreditation Commission of ABET; graduates are eligible to practice and become licensed professional engineers. Catalog notes (noted here only, never seeded): an additional 15 course credit hours beyond the 122 required for the degree will qualify graduates to apply for a postgraduate medical degree program; this program partners the BSEE Biomedical option with the MSEE degree — a maximum of 12 graduate-level credit hours can count toward both (ELEG 5313 Modern Control Systems can replace ELEG 4313 Modern Control Systems; ELEG 5113 Digital Signal Processing can replace ELEG 4113 Digital Signal Processing; ELEG 5153 Communication Systems II can replace ELEG 4153 Communication Systems II; ELEG 5133 Advanced Digital Design can replace ELEG 4133 Advanced Digital Design). The lecture/lab pairs (CHEM 2124 & CHEM 2120, CHEM 2134 & CHEM 2130, PHYS 2114 & PHYS 2000, PHYS 2124 & PHYS 2010, ELEG 2130 & ELEG 2134, COMS 1011 & COMS 1013) are printed as combined-hours lines and seeded as single slots. The catalog also lists courses NOT required for the Biomedical Option but recommended for application to an advanced medical degree program (15 hours total, noted here only, never seeded): Sophomore Fall BIOL 3034 Genetics (4); Spring CHEM 3264 Mechanistic Organic Chemistry (4); Junior Fall CHEM 3344 Principles of Biochemistry (4); Senior Spring BIOL 4033 Cell Biology (3). The catalog states the ordering is subject to change and advises a junior-year advisor planning session — noted here as context. Machine prereqs omitted (prereq: []) — the curriculum page prints no per-course prerequisites. tccns mirrors the local ATU course code; transfer_confidence core_only.",
